    <title>FastFrames: Video Generation at Interactive Latency</title>
    <link href="https://latifkedi.github.io/ahbar/?item=2026-11-18-11-fastframes-video-generation-at-interactive"/>
    <link rel="related" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.23226"/>
    <id>https://latifkedi.github.io/ahbar/item/2026-11-18-11-fastframes-video-generation-at-interactive</id>
    <updated>2026-11-16T19:00:00.000Z</updated>
    <summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;Autoregressive video diffusion models generate frames based on new observations and inputs, making them a promising medium for interactive visual experiences. However, existing models are orders of magnitude too slow for fluid interaction. This paper introduces FastFrames, a family of fast autoregressive video diffusion models that achieves interactive latency without compromising quality.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.23226&quot;&gt;Hugging Face Daily Papers&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;strong&gt;Tags:&lt;/strong&gt; #llm #open-weights #clean-tech #computer-vision&lt;/p&gt;</summary>
  </entry>
